Section: 2. Related Work
Text: The most recent project expanded on existing ideas for deﬁning offensive language and presented the OLID (Offensive Language Identiﬁcation Dataset), a corpus of Twitter posts hierarchically annotated on three levels, whether they contain offensive language or not, whether the offense is targeted and ﬁnally, the target of the offense (Zampieri et al., 2019a).

